WEBVTT

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:08.902 --> 01:10.528
If that's your plan,

01:11.654 --> 01:13.156
then forget the wishes.

01:14.032 --> 01:15.784
Just throw me off right now.

01:16.576 --> 01:17.410
I'm…

01:19.496 --> 01:22.874
having such fun!

01:25.376 --> 01:27.253
-You're having fun?
-Oh, yes.

01:28.171 --> 01:29.506
My life is so boring,

01:29.589 --> 01:32.926
and, oh, my heart's racing,
it feels so good.

01:35.804 --> 01:36.679
This is fun?

01:40.725 --> 01:43.645
Good. Then I'll make it
even more fun for you.

02:15.510 --> 02:16.886
It's the same scent.

02:18.513 --> 02:19.931
I'd know that clay anywhere.

02:21.057 --> 02:22.142
It's definitely you.

02:28.273 --> 02:29.816
This tells me I've grown lazy.

02:31.568 --> 02:33.486
Is this how corrupt humans have grown?

02:34.863 --> 02:36.865
Is there nothing
I can offer to tempt you with?

02:37.907 --> 02:40.910
What was it like when you fell?
Can you feel anything?

02:42.120 --> 02:43.997
I could join you in your ways.

02:44.080 --> 02:47.167
Can I try to kill you before you kill me?
Let's see who's the better killer.

02:53.715 --> 02:54.924
I am warning you.

02:56.467 --> 02:59.095
if you ever put a hand on me again…

02:59.179 --> 03:00.930
…then all humans except you

03:01.681 --> 03:05.852
will be torn limb from limb and crushed
from the oldest to the youngest.

03:07.228 --> 03:09.856
I'll put to death and butcher
every last bit of life,

03:10.732 --> 03:11.816
sparing no soul.

03:14.027 --> 03:16.029
I'll go to those extremes
to make you suffer.

03:19.490 --> 03:22.493
I already put you in my plans
983 years ago.

03:25.663 --> 03:26.623
Wait.

03:27.248 --> 03:28.917
You're leaving me like this?

03:29.500 --> 03:31.544
How am I supposed to get down? Hey!

03:47.185 --> 03:49.187
Four wheels.

03:50.855 --> 03:53.566
So those are what Sade said
roll around on their own.

04:21.094 --> 04:23.304
That's my beast, Sade, the jaguar.

04:26.307 --> 04:29.269
Oh! My master!
How long have you been out for?

04:30.061 --> 04:31.020
Get out.

04:31.104 --> 04:33.856
I would love to,
but I'm being watched right now.

04:33.940 --> 04:36.776
I'll meet you at the oasis
as soon as I'm able to.

04:36.859 --> 04:37.944
I'll be there soon.

04:38.027 --> 04:40.905
I've changed a lot,
so don't be too surprised, okay?

04:40.989 --> 04:42.407
Get over here now.

04:44.325 --> 04:47.078
I was born
from a single tear that glistened

04:47.161 --> 04:51.958
as it was shed on a strand
of my master's jet-black hair.

04:52.041 --> 04:56.629
If you understand what I'm saying,
that's because…

04:56.713 --> 04:59.048
What are you going on about?
Get over here.

05:01.259 --> 05:03.469
It's been so long.
I've missed you, Master.

05:03.553 --> 05:06.055
Oh. Oh, your scent…

05:07.098 --> 05:10.351
Cut it out. You served
other masters happily, didn't you?

05:10.435 --> 05:12.312
I only did it to survive.

05:12.395 --> 05:14.731
Take a look. Things now have become fancy.

05:15.398 --> 05:16.733
The oasis is even a hotel.

05:18.401 --> 05:20.862
New laws like animal protection
have prohibited hunting,

05:20.945 --> 05:22.572
so I'm basically an herbivore.

05:32.290 --> 05:33.583
Anyway, did you get hurt?

05:33.666 --> 05:36.044
It kind of felt like
my head was splitting earlier.

05:37.587 --> 05:39.088
There kind of was an incident.

05:41.132 --> 05:44.969
Could my head injury
be the reason you look so…

05:45.053 --> 05:45.970
What's wrong?

05:46.554 --> 05:48.556
Oh, right, this is the first time
you're seeing it.

05:48.639 --> 05:50.641
This is the special face I told you about.

05:52.352 --> 05:53.269
What?

05:53.353 --> 05:55.980
Ah, I need to get you up to speed
on the latest trends.

05:56.064 --> 05:58.858
Hey, a new master
has released you from the lamp.

05:58.941 --> 05:59.942
How are they?

06:00.026 --> 06:02.779
-They the type who'll want extra wishes?
-Not at all.

06:02.862 --> 06:04.614
Actually, they've not made any.

06:05.448 --> 06:07.075
I don't know. It's bizarre.

06:55.289 --> 06:56.124
Mmm.

06:57.583 --> 06:58.668
What are you doing here?

06:58.751 --> 06:59.585
Mmm.

07:00.420 --> 07:02.922
This is the first ride
on this type of carpet for me.

07:03.005 --> 07:04.841
The food, oh, it's scrumptious.

07:06.926 --> 07:08.594
So you abandoned your genie this morning.

07:08.678 --> 07:10.388
I only left you at the hotel.

07:10.471 --> 07:11.514
That's abandonment.

07:11.597 --> 07:12.932
No, I just left you there.

07:15.351 --> 07:17.937
I see we'll never engage
in a proper discussion.

07:18.020 --> 07:19.605
But you can't get rid of me.

07:21.482 --> 07:22.900
So don't waste your energy.

07:27.321 --> 07:30.158
I've had enough to eat. I need a nap.
See you in Goryeo.

07:35.830 --> 07:37.582
This is beyond annoying.

07:38.708 --> 07:40.042
All right then. Okay.

07:41.377 --> 07:43.713
Stop wearing your hair up
in a bun like mine, all right?

07:43.796 --> 07:46.716
It's too similar to my hairstyle,
so you might as well cut it.

07:46.799 --> 07:49.594
I spend so much energy on it.
I use daily hair mask.

07:49.677 --> 07:51.554
I demand you change it. You hear me?

07:57.018 --> 07:59.645
-Mmm.
-Wait until it gets crispy.

07:59.729 --> 08:01.022
I'm back.

08:01.772 --> 08:02.773
Oh, my.

08:04.984 --> 08:06.068
-What now?
-Ah.

08:06.152 --> 08:09.697
I thought Ka-young seemed prettier lately.
Now I see you're dating.

08:09.780 --> 08:11.449
-Makes sense.
-Who's dating?

08:11.532 --> 08:12.909
I'm always very pretty, Grandma.

08:12.992 --> 08:16.329
Okay, but who's this
lanky fellow with you?

08:18.122 --> 08:18.956
Hi.

08:23.044 --> 08:25.963
Not a single word from you.
And I'm serious.

08:27.131 --> 08:28.799
He's a memento, a keepsake.

08:29.467 --> 08:33.304
That's Grandma An,
Grandma Park, Grandma Sa,

08:33.888 --> 08:34.722
and my grandma.

08:34.805 --> 08:37.517
How incredible.
What great news. That's wonderful.

08:37.600 --> 08:40.520
She went overseas and brought home
a potential husband. Hmm?

08:40.603 --> 08:42.438
He's not a potential anything.

08:42.522 --> 08:43.439
We're just…

08:44.273 --> 08:45.233
rooming together.

08:45.316 --> 08:46.400
Huh?

08:47.026 --> 08:49.237
Once you share a room,
it can only lead to, well…

08:49.320 --> 08:51.322
You need Granny to tell you.

08:51.405 --> 08:52.907
Who knows what could happen?

08:53.783 --> 08:55.701
Pan-geum. Great-grandbabies are in your--

08:55.785 --> 08:57.286
That's enough. Stop.

08:59.664 --> 09:00.665
Are you hungry?

09:01.749 --> 09:04.460
-I'm An Bok-ja. We're glad you're here.
-Yes, thanks.

09:04.544 --> 09:06.003
I'm Lee Beu-li.

09:06.087 --> 09:08.464
-A good name, don't you think?
-"Lee Beu-li"?

09:09.507 --> 09:10.800
-Lee Beu-li?
-Lee Beu-li?

09:13.094 --> 09:14.387
Come with me.

09:15.137 --> 09:17.473
Why would they go to the shed?
The bedroom is further down.

09:19.225 --> 09:20.685
Oh, stop that right now.

09:21.185 --> 09:23.437
What has gotten into you?
The food will burn. Flip it.

09:23.521 --> 09:25.022
It's perfect. Extra crispy.

09:27.066 --> 09:27.984
"Lee Beu-li"?

09:30.820 --> 09:32.154
My research showed me

09:32.238 --> 09:34.490
that all the names here
have three syllables.

09:35.324 --> 09:36.951
An Bok-ja, Ki Ka-young,

09:37.743 --> 09:38.661
Lee Beu-li.

09:39.579 --> 09:41.455
All right, you figured that out.

09:42.248 --> 09:43.165
Congrats, but…

09:44.917 --> 09:47.336
Forget it. Keep it. It's your name. Okay.

09:47.420 --> 09:48.838
Let's go over the rules.

09:48.921 --> 09:52.258
All grandmas, you stay away from.
Stay out of sight of the locals too.

09:52.341 --> 09:53.759
No magic around anyone.

09:53.843 --> 09:55.094
No mention of me making wishes.

09:55.177 --> 09:58.347
And don't even think about
going into town for any business.

09:58.848 --> 09:59.765
Okay?

10:00.433 --> 10:01.684
What am I supposed to do?

10:02.852 --> 10:04.353
I've come all this way to do what?

10:05.021 --> 10:08.107
You say you want to try killing me,
then make a wish to do it.

10:08.190 --> 10:10.818
-That's your hope, right?
-Using a wish for that would be a waste.

10:10.901 --> 10:11.736
I could just do it.

10:17.199 --> 10:18.743
What are you muttering?

10:20.620 --> 10:22.371
Where did the lanky fellow go?

10:24.248 --> 10:26.375
Why are you holding a pickaxe?

10:28.294 --> 10:31.631
-You're only visible to me now?
-You told me to stay away from grandmas.

10:32.340 --> 10:34.842
What's going on? What is it?
Are you seeing things, Ka-young?

10:34.925 --> 10:36.344
You taking your meds?

10:39.555 --> 10:41.098
Grandma, cover both ears.

10:41.641 --> 10:43.893
-This thing has to die right now.
-Die? What?

10:43.976 --> 10:45.728
Who do you want to kill?

10:45.811 --> 10:47.855
Ka-young,
remember your promise to me, okay?

10:47.938 --> 10:49.607
The rules still stand.

10:58.699 --> 10:59.909
I know.

11:21.555 --> 11:24.809
Ka-young. Your mom, dad,
and older sisters…

11:25.393 --> 11:28.270
They aren't returning. They've all died.

11:29.105 --> 11:30.314
Why did they all die?

11:30.398 --> 11:31.982
I only killed my mom's parrot.

11:33.275 --> 11:37.113
Mom, Dad, and my older sisters,
I never killed them.

11:37.196 --> 11:38.030
I know.

11:38.739 --> 11:40.366
Grandma understands.

11:41.242 --> 11:44.161
You won't kill anyone or anything at all
from now on.

11:45.162 --> 11:46.997
Not birds or other animals, okay?

11:47.498 --> 11:50.084
We must live a long life together.
Understand?

11:52.294 --> 11:53.713
But they said they'd come back.

11:53.796 --> 11:55.297
They promised they would!

11:58.259 --> 12:01.137
I didn't give them permission!
Why did they die?

12:15.735 --> 12:18.738
Listen. From now on,
when you get angry, you do this.

12:19.655 --> 12:21.866
Close your eyes
and listen to grandma's watch.

12:21.949 --> 12:23.367
It's saying "ticktock," right?

12:23.951 --> 12:27.955
Listen to that sound for a minute.
Sixty ticks. Sixty ticks make one minute.

12:28.539 --> 12:32.168
Get off! No way!
I'm still angry. It hurts inside.

12:32.251 --> 12:36.464
Then you must listen for two minutes.
Keep your focus on it, okay?

12:37.381 --> 12:38.674
I hate this!

12:38.758 --> 12:40.468
Put it away! Stop it now!

12:42.011 --> 12:45.431
I hate your stupid watch!
I don't want this!

12:48.017 --> 12:49.226
KA-YOUNG'S STUDY COMPILATION 1

12:49.310 --> 12:50.352
728…

12:50.436 --> 12:51.812
Mr. Chang-sik made this.

12:51.896 --> 12:55.274
Let's watch this special video.
Let's watch it together.

12:55.357 --> 12:58.027
My goodness. This is so fun, right?

12:58.110 --> 13:00.070
Congratulations. It's a baby girl.

13:00.154 --> 13:01.864
-Here you go.
-Oh, Chae-a.

13:01.947 --> 13:04.033
-757. 758.
-Sweet girl.

13:04.116 --> 13:06.076
-You see that, Ka-young?
-Oh, yes.

13:06.160 --> 13:09.580
That grandma and father are happy.
Look how proud and happy they are.

13:10.122 --> 13:11.749
That is happiness.

13:11.832 --> 13:15.294
-765, 766, 767…
-I love you so much.

13:15.377 --> 13:18.130
…768, 769…

13:18.214 --> 13:19.673
We did everything we could,

13:19.757 --> 13:23.093
but unfortunately,
the mother has passed away in childbirth.

13:23.177 --> 13:24.804
What?

13:24.887 --> 13:27.014
Oh, my. How very sad.

13:27.765 --> 13:28.849
That's real despair.

13:28.933 --> 13:30.267
They've lost a mother.

13:31.185 --> 13:32.937
Such a dear person they love.

13:33.020 --> 13:35.439
…779, 780…

13:36.774 --> 13:39.944
Dad, you can't let go, okay?
You just can't. Hold on tight.

13:40.027 --> 13:41.987
I am, of course. Daddy's holding on tight.

13:42.071 --> 13:43.989
-Dad, you didn't let go, right?
-No, I haven't.

13:44.073 --> 13:46.909
-You're still holding on?
-Why, you did it!

13:46.992 --> 13:48.828
-Yay, Chae-a!
-Hurray!

13:49.578 --> 13:51.789
That right there is real happiness.

13:51.872 --> 13:53.499
Slow down. Go slow.

13:53.582 --> 13:56.669
You want to ride a bike?
You might like it if you try it.

13:56.752 --> 13:59.964
…797, 798…

14:01.590 --> 14:03.384
In Ka-young's case, ma'am,

14:03.467 --> 14:05.469
trying to teach her
how to regulate herself

14:05.553 --> 14:06.679
would waste your time.

14:06.762 --> 14:09.974
…806, 807, 808,

14:10.057 --> 14:12.268
809, 810…

14:12.768 --> 14:14.854
-…811, 812…
-This is…

14:14.937 --> 14:15.855
affection.

14:17.147 --> 14:18.566
Nice and cozy, right?

14:18.649 --> 14:20.067
…815, 816…

14:20.150 --> 14:22.027
She doesn't have a sense of guilt,

14:22.111 --> 14:24.822
and she's unable to control
her deep rage at the world.

14:24.905 --> 14:27.741
Oh. Ka-young is so warm.

14:27.825 --> 14:30.578
…826, 827,

14:30.661 --> 14:33.163
-828, 829…
-Oh.

14:33.247 --> 14:35.374
Our little rascal is so brave.

14:35.457 --> 14:39.670
…831, 832, 833,

14:39.753 --> 14:42.840
-834, 835…
-Ah, you…

14:42.923 --> 14:45.759
-…836, 837…
-Our stubborn darling is so warm.

14:45.843 --> 14:48.679
…838, 839,

14:48.762 --> 14:53.100
840, 841, 842…

15:01.775 --> 15:04.445
I told you to always keep that stone in.

15:06.989 --> 15:10.743
You can't take it out until tomorrow
even if the sky falls.

15:11.744 --> 15:12.578
Good.

15:13.787 --> 15:16.624
Why should I? Why do I have to?

15:16.707 --> 15:17.750
It's uncomfortable.

15:17.833 --> 15:21.921
It should be. That's right.
That's exactly what discomfort is.

15:22.004 --> 15:25.299
When other people look at you
with their eyes all narrow,

15:25.382 --> 15:27.134
it's because they're uncomfortable.

15:27.217 --> 15:29.303
It's not because they don't like you.

15:29.386 --> 15:31.555
It's because they don't get you.
All right?

15:31.639 --> 15:34.808
Stop talking so much, Grandma.
You're so annoying.

15:35.309 --> 15:37.519
What do I have to do
to stop living with you?

15:39.438 --> 15:43.067
If you study really hard
and attend college,

15:43.150 --> 15:44.652
you won't have to live with me.

15:44.735 --> 15:48.739
You need to practice and study.
It takes hard work to be good.

15:48.822 --> 15:50.824
You have to be the top of the class.

16:00.000 --> 16:02.002
Once you get to the top of the class…

16:02.086 --> 16:04.338
KI KA-YOUNG
TOP ADMISSION SCORE

16:04.421 --> 16:05.798
…you must attend a famous college.

16:05.881 --> 16:08.467
It's no small feat
to get accepted into a top university.

16:08.550 --> 16:10.678
Once you graduate from college,

16:10.761 --> 16:13.973
you need to get a job
that pays a good, steady paycheck.

16:15.724 --> 16:17.601
Thanks for this. Congratulations.

16:17.685 --> 16:19.770
-Oh, great, thank you.
-Congratulations.

16:19.853 --> 16:21.188
Thank you. Congratulations.

16:21.271 --> 16:22.773
What a great location.

16:23.691 --> 16:25.609
KI KA-YOUNG
TOP ADMISSION SCORE

16:28.988 --> 16:30.906
She makes the town proud,

16:30.990 --> 16:33.575
but at the same time,
she's the village fool.

16:34.159 --> 16:35.786
-How's she both?
-Both?

16:37.371 --> 16:39.999
So, what college did you go to?

16:42.126 --> 16:45.295
We didn't even discuss college at all.

16:45.838 --> 16:50.342
I mean, the thing is,
I can't really freely go around anywhere.

16:50.426 --> 16:54.013
Even so, having the same schooling
is better for a relationship.

16:54.096 --> 16:56.765
Ka-young was accepted
into one of the best schools

16:56.849 --> 16:59.226
with top grades and graduated early.

16:59.810 --> 17:00.811
Did you graduate?

17:02.104 --> 17:04.273
Uh…

17:07.693 --> 17:09.611
What were your test scores?

17:13.615 --> 17:16.326
Your grandma's really on fire.
She's ready to roast me.

17:16.827 --> 17:18.454
-Why?
-It's your fault.

17:19.455 --> 17:21.832
You must have said something
about achieving similar things.

17:21.915 --> 17:22.916
Don't do that again.

17:23.000 --> 17:24.168
She seemed frustrated.

17:26.086 --> 17:27.629
Hmm?

17:34.762 --> 17:36.638
-Don't bother.
-Really?

17:39.141 --> 17:40.309
Mmm.

17:43.395 --> 17:44.938
It's none of your business.

17:52.905 --> 17:54.823
You're pretty strong.

17:59.036 --> 17:59.870
Humans.

18:00.704 --> 18:02.498
I guess that's how I look to you.

18:03.582 --> 18:05.042
THIS BOZO'S FIRST TIME SEEING THOR

18:05.125 --> 18:07.461
-Mmm. I'm the one with the hammer?
-That's not you.

18:08.462 --> 18:11.465
You sure? We have the same haircut. Then…

18:11.548 --> 18:13.050
CAPTAIN AMERICA JUST PASSED BY

18:13.133 --> 18:14.468
He's buff, brave, and brawny.

18:14.551 --> 18:15.969
-With a star too.
-No, wrong again.

18:16.720 --> 18:18.222
Well, then…

18:18.305 --> 18:20.557
-The powerful one in the red metal suit.
-No way.

18:20.641 --> 18:22.518
No way. Not even close.

18:23.143 --> 18:25.562
These are Mar**l
characters. You're Dis**y.

18:25.646 --> 18:27.564
It's an entirely different
target audience.

18:27.648 --> 18:29.399
These characters aren't you.

18:29.483 --> 18:31.819
The two universes don't belong together.

18:32.319 --> 18:33.987
We'll never talk about this again.

18:35.280 --> 18:37.741
Come on. I couldn't even hear
what you were saying.

18:37.825 --> 18:40.702
The beeps were too loud
to hear what you were talking about.

18:40.786 --> 18:42.121
You may be a genie,

18:42.955 --> 18:45.165
you still cannot
infringe on copyright.

18:46.083 --> 18:49.169
-Franchises are a serious enterprise.
-Franchise?

18:49.253 --> 18:50.504
If you want to know more,

18:50.587 --> 18:54.174
then you should write to the studios
and get their permission yourself. Hmph.

18:55.467 --> 18:59.221
In what world would I need permission?
You forget I'm a real genie or what?

18:59.721 --> 19:00.722
What are you saying, huh?

19:04.685 --> 19:06.520
-Is this a modern-day arena?
-Yes.

19:06.603 --> 19:09.398
And I have three identities
that shape public opinion.

19:11.984 --> 19:13.986
-Do you trust me?
-Sure.

19:15.445 --> 19:17.114
I'm gonna make a post.

19:17.197 --> 19:19.449
This IP business is ridiculous,

19:19.533 --> 19:23.537
and copyright laws have made it impossible
to talk about certain franchises.

19:23.620 --> 19:24.955
It doesn't make any sense.

19:25.038 --> 19:27.207
Seriously, like, I'm the genie here,

19:27.291 --> 19:30.294
and apparently,
there's a movie about me called Aladdin.

19:30.377 --> 19:32.129
-I don't get it.
-You brat.

19:32.212 --> 19:34.506
I never met a guy named Aladdin.

19:34.590 --> 19:36.508
Get your story right.
Upvote if you can relate.

19:36.592 --> 19:37.885
What's this arena forum called?

19:39.803 --> 19:41.847
-Mate Pann.
-"Mate Pann."

19:42.347 --> 19:45.225
See this? They've gone wild
in this section.

19:45.309 --> 19:47.644
I said, trust me, Master. Now look.

19:47.728 --> 19:49.313
You did.

19:49.396 --> 19:51.565
A GENIE ON MATE PANN?
GO TOUCH GRASS, BRO

19:51.648 --> 19:53.358
WE NEED ALADDIN'S SIDE OF THE STORY

19:53.442 --> 19:55.444
BIG CAP, GO SEEK HELP

19:55.527 --> 19:57.362
-Wait. Why am I getting criticized?
-Oh…

19:57.446 --> 19:59.072
Oh, uh…

20:02.034 --> 20:04.119
Huh? You're a silly boy,
wasting your time.

20:04.203 --> 20:06.538
Wait, did you… You're able to read Korean?

20:08.540 --> 20:12.044
Mr. Seo I-deuk. You're here?
But you're supposed to chop wood for us.

20:12.127 --> 20:14.796
I was just headed there, well, but now…

20:14.880 --> 20:16.632
-Have you eaten? I'm hungry.
-Hmm?

20:17.132 --> 20:18.467
Sit before I get angry.

20:18.550 --> 20:20.219
Your place is with me.

20:20.302 --> 20:21.136
Who's that?

20:22.054 --> 20:24.348
-Do you know him, Mr. Seo?
-I'm sort of…

20:24.431 --> 20:27.059
We're catching up.
It's been almost a thousand years.

20:27.142 --> 20:28.143
Well, let's get going.

20:28.227 --> 20:30.562
-We'll go. Let's go, go, go.
-I told you to sit down.

20:30.646 --> 20:32.189
Sit down this instant!

20:32.689 --> 20:34.691
-Whoa!
-What just happened?

20:34.775 --> 20:37.486
I need to restart, reboot it!

20:37.569 --> 20:40.239
Who the fuck did this?
I'll kill them for what happened.

20:40.322 --> 20:42.324
Son of a… I was just about to level up!

20:42.407 --> 20:43.700
Shit! What the fuck?

20:47.788 --> 20:48.622
Oh, look, wow!

20:51.166 --> 20:53.418
The trees in the forest
will no longer exist.

20:53.502 --> 20:56.588
He's the wild, hunky fellow
staying at Sang-tae's guesthouse.

20:56.672 --> 20:58.840
Oh, bravo. He's quite something.

21:18.610 --> 21:20.153
-These lettuces are good…
-Oh, my.

21:20.237 --> 21:22.072
There's a stupidly expensive car
coming here.

21:22.155 --> 21:22.990
What?

21:24.241 --> 21:26.743
Oh, right. It's owned by the psycho.

21:26.827 --> 21:28.954
Huh? What would make you say that?

21:30.497 --> 21:31.581
Hello, you two.

21:32.416 --> 21:35.627
-She could've heard.
-That's all right. She knows it all.

21:35.711 --> 21:38.714
Oh, yes. Hello!
Keep driving that car, maniac!

21:38.797 --> 21:42.175
She has one of those anti-psycho character
disorders or something like that.

21:42.259 --> 21:45.053
It's antisocial personality disorder,
Grandma.

21:45.137 --> 21:47.097
And always apply sunscreen.

21:48.390 --> 21:49.308
Yes. Okay.

21:50.976 --> 21:54.354
When you say psychopath,
do you mean the ones who kill people?

21:54.438 --> 21:56.315
Don't worry. She's not a murderer.

21:56.898 --> 22:00.110
We saved her from that
because we all raised her together.

22:00.193 --> 22:01.862
How did you raise her?

22:01.945 --> 22:04.531
-Why'd you pop up like that?
-How'd you get here?

22:05.115 --> 22:06.074
This is very strange.

22:06.158 --> 22:09.161
Oh, I see.
It's just the psycho's potential husband.

22:09.244 --> 22:11.997
-That's right. So how did you raise her?
-Oh, that?

22:12.706 --> 22:14.416
It was a huge problem at first,

22:14.499 --> 22:17.294
worse than anything
that could have ever been imagined.

22:22.132 --> 22:24.634
This is the number 7.

22:26.303 --> 22:27.304
This is the letter…

22:28.263 --> 22:29.306
"L," you see?

22:32.059 --> 22:35.103
This is the letter "C,"
the third letter in the alphabet.

22:37.439 --> 22:39.775
It gets more challenging
with other letters.

22:39.858 --> 22:40.942
Are you ready for it?

23:19.898 --> 23:21.733
Oh, my goodness. Oh…

23:21.817 --> 23:23.235
Okay. All right. I'll do it.

23:24.694 --> 23:27.906
Let me show you.
Eat this first so you know the texture.

23:27.989 --> 23:30.992
Slice it gently like this.
Hold the knife by the rice cake.

23:31.076 --> 23:33.120
And so, it was the entire village

23:33.203 --> 23:36.289
that came together
to help raise that little devil.

23:36.373 --> 23:38.583
-Hold it like that. Good.
-Devil, huh?

23:38.667 --> 23:40.877
Push and that's it.
You got it. There you go.

23:40.961 --> 23:41.878
But are you?

23:52.431 --> 23:55.434
-You're busy, are you?
-I'm done soon. How may I help you?

23:56.184 --> 23:58.770
I broke a taillight while parking.
Can you fix it?

24:07.612 --> 24:10.365
If you change the taillight,
the truck bed can stay like this?

24:10.449 --> 24:11.867
The back's really loaded up.

24:12.492 --> 24:13.702
Yeah, it's fine.

24:13.785 --> 24:15.829
Come back later before 6:00.
That's when I close.

24:16.788 --> 24:19.791
I'll leave it with you.
I'm going to my mom's restaurant.

24:29.050 --> 24:29.885
Phew.

24:35.098 --> 24:38.018
Aw, man, you started without me?

24:39.561 --> 24:42.189
I got extra food.
If you need more, it's all yours.

24:42.272 --> 24:43.523
-Thank you.
-Thank you so much.

24:43.607 --> 24:44.483
Thank you very much.

24:44.566 --> 24:47.027
By the way, the Wi-Fi connection
is really slow and bad.

24:47.110 --> 24:49.321
-Is that normal?
-We're in the mountains.

24:49.404 --> 24:52.282
See it as a break away from the bustle
of your busy city lives.

24:52.365 --> 24:53.241
Oh.

24:53.325 --> 24:55.660
He's right.
I-deuk doesn't even have a phone.

24:56.620 --> 24:59.372
Oh, I-deuk!
Stop shopping and come eat with us.

24:59.456 --> 25:02.042
I don't like eating cooked meat.
I like it raw.

25:02.125 --> 25:03.210
Go ahead. Enjoy.

25:08.882 --> 25:12.844
Shopping list. Chili powder,
bean sprouts, pain-relief patches,

25:12.928 --> 25:14.262
tofu, and bread.

25:15.847 --> 25:16.765
What in the world?

25:17.390 --> 25:19.935
-Those look so cool.
-I told you, you can't come into town.

25:20.018 --> 25:22.479
Let's get two of those.
Wait, three of those.

25:50.674 --> 25:53.009
I heard that you're here
and brought a potential hubby.

25:53.093 --> 25:54.261
Is that him?

25:54.344 --> 25:56.846
Hello, again.
He's not a potential anything.

25:56.930 --> 25:58.473
-Don't speak or breathe.
-Oh.

26:00.100 --> 26:02.310
How can you tell me he's not what he is?

26:04.396 --> 26:07.065
The neighborhood's gonna need
some rice to throw.

26:07.649 --> 26:09.150
Let me introduce myself.

26:09.234 --> 26:12.571
The village chief here
at Cheongpung Village, Park Chang-sik.

26:13.363 --> 26:16.241
Here are my interns,
Jwa Jong-heon and Woo Min-jae.

26:17.033 --> 26:18.868
-Say hello.
-Nice to meet ya.

26:18.952 --> 26:21.580
You're as tall as a skyscraper.
You must drink milk.

26:21.663 --> 26:23.873
It's nice here, isn't it?

26:23.957 --> 26:25.083
It's because of our Ka-young

26:25.166 --> 26:27.377
that our village never has to worry
about public safety.

26:27.460 --> 26:29.462
She keeps criminals away. She does.

26:31.339 --> 26:33.216
Why am I the only one talking?

26:35.093 --> 26:36.720
Am I the only one with a mouth?

26:37.804 --> 26:39.472
The only one happy we're meeting?

26:41.349 --> 26:42.350
Greet them.

26:43.059 --> 26:44.811
-Keep it quick.
-Sure thing.

26:45.854 --> 26:46.771
Nice to meet you.

26:46.855 --> 26:49.357
So you're the big chief
of this amazing village.

26:49.941 --> 26:52.777
It's good to meet the big fish here,
Park Chang-sik.

27:07.751 --> 27:09.002
What happened?

27:09.085 --> 27:10.629
What's the meaning of this?

27:11.171 --> 27:13.923
Calm down, please.
Relax, or you could end up dead.

27:14.007 --> 27:16.051
What did you do? Why is my nose buzzing?

27:18.053 --> 27:20.722
What made you do that?
Why do you find me so tempting?

27:21.222 --> 27:24.434
-Use your words. Relax. Keep it calm--
-Let go of me! I told you to let go!

27:24.517 --> 27:25.644
Oh, damn it!

27:25.727 --> 27:27.228
Goddammit!

27:27.312 --> 27:28.146
What the…

27:28.772 --> 27:30.273
-Hmm?
-Where did he go?

27:32.192 --> 27:33.610
Did he already run off?

27:41.201 --> 27:43.286
Oh, what just happened?

27:43.370 --> 27:44.788
Where is he?

27:45.372 --> 27:46.790
Oh, no, where did he go?

27:46.873 --> 27:48.041
Huh?

27:48.124 --> 27:50.335
Oh, where could he have gone?

27:51.294 --> 27:52.128
Tsk.

27:52.212 --> 27:54.255
CHEONGPUNGHO MART

27:54.339 --> 27:57.884
How many times do you need to hear that
the display at the entrance is important?

27:57.967 --> 28:00.845
Why is it important?
It's the main face of our store.

28:00.929 --> 28:02.055
Don't keep it so bare.

28:02.847 --> 28:03.682
Understand?

28:04.683 --> 28:06.226
Are you even listening?

28:07.602 --> 28:08.603
I apologize.

28:09.312 --> 28:12.315
The big things are hard to carry
while the elevator's broken.

28:12.816 --> 28:13.900
Kang Im-seon.

28:14.401 --> 28:17.404
Our building has many stairs.
Don't your feet work?

28:18.530 --> 28:20.532
Oh. I'm very sorry. I'll get on it.

28:28.248 --> 28:31.584
Men don't rub noses like that
in this country. That's another rule.

28:32.502 --> 28:34.170
Huh? What is this place?

28:35.714 --> 28:36.923
What is all this?

28:37.674 --> 28:39.300
Whoa.

28:40.427 --> 28:42.429
Is this for everyone?

28:43.138 --> 28:44.347
Stop running around.

28:46.307 --> 28:48.810
Do you see him? Sorry.
Can you tell me if there's a man there?

28:49.769 --> 28:52.772
Oh, yes, he's quite handsome. Why?

28:53.398 --> 28:55.859
Uh, I just wondered
if he's handsome to others.

28:55.942 --> 28:56.943
Thank you so much.

29:01.364 --> 29:02.365
Chief Park's macho.

29:02.449 --> 29:05.493
He's a former Marine
whose motto is "Dignity above all."

29:05.577 --> 29:06.911
You're now his target.

29:06.995 --> 29:09.080
What are you going to do
about being wanted?

29:10.749 --> 29:12.500
Did I hear you right?
You think I look good?

29:12.584 --> 29:14.919
I don't feel emotions, but I have eyes.

29:16.463 --> 29:18.506
What do you mean? No emotions?

29:18.590 --> 29:21.551
Don't let Min-ji catch you.
You need to be careful around her.

29:21.634 --> 29:23.261
Her rules are much harsher.

29:24.179 --> 29:25.597
Huh? Min-ji? Who's that?

29:32.520 --> 29:35.732
Excuse me, sir.
That's the ladies' restroom, please.

29:36.357 --> 29:39.152
-Yes, I know.
-I'm so very sorry.

29:39.235 --> 29:42.155
-Please accept my apology.
-It's fine. I get that often.

30:00.256 --> 30:01.591
Don't worry, I'm female.

30:02.217 --> 30:03.051
I know that.

30:03.134 --> 30:05.970
The Smile Dental Clinic's
your business, right?

30:07.889 --> 30:09.057
We know each other?

30:10.809 --> 30:13.228
Ah, yes. Now I remember.

30:13.812 --> 30:16.898
When I signed the lease.
You work for Ryu Su-hyeon.

30:17.774 --> 30:20.151
Did you play today?
The golf's great, don't you think?

30:21.277 --> 30:22.779
I'll tell that to the owner.

30:22.862 --> 30:25.240
You've met him.
Mr. Ryu bought this golf course.

30:25.323 --> 30:28.201
This one as well? Whoa.

30:28.284 --> 30:31.913
He's successful, but he still finds time
to volunteer at food banks.

30:32.497 --> 30:35.416
One of his buildings
was just finished recently, right?

30:45.260 --> 30:47.512
The floors that have already been sold

30:47.595 --> 30:49.347
can be moved in to starting next week.

30:49.430 --> 30:52.475
-That's good news.
-I'm relieved to hear that you agree.

30:52.559 --> 30:55.061
I'm having a hard time
with the amount of paperwork,

30:55.144 --> 30:56.563
so it's good that you approve.

30:57.313 --> 30:59.691
Although, I wonder
what makes you buy more stuff

30:59.774 --> 31:01.359
when you already have so much.

31:04.362 --> 31:06.739
Living this way as a human is like

31:06.823 --> 31:09.409
setting foot in a living hell
even if it isn't hell itself.

31:10.326 --> 31:12.370
If you got no money, that's extra hellish.

31:13.329 --> 31:14.873
Hell isn't a place for me.

31:20.712 --> 31:22.714
First time you met him, you rubbed noses?

31:22.797 --> 31:24.507
Well, at least you're still alive.

31:25.091 --> 31:28.136
But better drink up.
Things might go south.

31:40.440 --> 31:41.691
Ah!

31:43.860 --> 31:47.071
This aluminum kettle thing is amazing.

31:47.155 --> 31:48.239
Extraordinary.

31:48.323 --> 31:50.241
Aluminum, you know, but…

31:50.325 --> 31:51.618
…cans are a mystery.

31:51.701 --> 31:52.619
GOBLIN STATIONERY

31:52.702 --> 31:54.913
Wow. This can…

31:54.996 --> 31:56.664
Sit here and wait for a while.

31:57.206 --> 31:59.876
Uh… I'll come back when I'm done
with my after-school job.

31:59.959 --> 32:02.086
Hey, why do you go around helping others?

32:02.170 --> 32:05.006
You're the mythical beast of Satan.
Be the destroyer.

32:05.089 --> 32:08.259
Wait here and stop spouting nonsense.
It's infuriating.

32:09.010 --> 32:10.011
What?

32:14.766 --> 32:16.517
Ready, go!

32:19.437 --> 32:20.647
What kind of lamp is this?

32:21.940 --> 32:23.232
K.O.!

32:23.316 --> 32:24.484
What sorcery?

32:32.283 --> 32:35.536
Huh? You're still playing there?

32:35.620 --> 32:38.373
-Let's go!
-I would love to, but I can't.

32:39.040 --> 32:41.334
My mission is here.

32:41.417 --> 32:43.169
I'll be trapped in this forever.

32:47.298 --> 32:48.508
Ah!

32:56.015 --> 32:58.518
If I wanna win,
I need to work on my combo game.

33:00.937 --> 33:03.648
-K.O.!
-Ugh!

33:12.323 --> 33:14.283
Ugh! Ah!

33:15.785 --> 33:17.036
You stay put right here.

33:17.120 --> 33:19.455
Sure, I'll wait. I love a good challenge.

33:33.970 --> 33:35.346
Oh, it's beautiful.

33:49.068 --> 33:50.903
Excuse me, miss. Hey, there.

33:51.487 --> 33:53.740
Step back. It's dangerous there.

33:56.868 --> 33:58.703
-Yes, I know.
-Just let her be.

33:58.786 --> 34:00.788
She's an experienced hiker like we are.

34:00.872 --> 34:02.415
-She's on the same path as us.
-Oh!

34:02.498 --> 34:05.209
It's the young lady
who picks up the trash.

34:05.293 --> 34:07.712
Oh, my, my. Nice to see you here.

34:07.795 --> 34:10.173
I've heard a lot about you.

34:10.256 --> 34:11.090
Yes, I know.

34:16.095 --> 34:17.972
You took so long to get down!

34:19.015 --> 34:21.100
What are you doing? You knew I was here?

34:22.018 --> 34:25.063
I'm begging you. One buck.
This is the last time, I swear.

34:25.146 --> 34:28.316
You ran all this way for one buck?
You're a genie, aren't you?

34:28.399 --> 34:29.734
Just make some of your own money.

34:29.817 --> 34:32.945
Genies aren't allowed to make treasures
for their own purposes.

34:33.029 --> 34:34.614
I only ask for the money.

34:34.697 --> 34:36.532
Make your wishes.

34:36.616 --> 34:38.242
You have three. Make them prompt.

34:38.326 --> 34:40.328
Wish them now. Or give me the money.

34:40.411 --> 34:42.747
You came for short change?

34:43.456 --> 34:45.416
Wait. You said it's the last time.

34:45.500 --> 34:47.627
That means there was a first.
How did you--

34:47.710 --> 34:49.629
I didn't steal it.
I borrowed it from Pan-geum.

34:50.505 --> 34:51.339
You think

34:51.422 --> 34:53.257
stealing from an old lady is okay?

34:53.341 --> 34:56.803
Why does she always have a weapon?
Be civil! Use words!

34:56.886 --> 34:59.180
Come here, you dirty thief!

34:59.263 --> 35:02.183
Give it back!
Give back my grandma's money!

35:11.275 --> 35:15.321
JUST ONE BUCK!

35:35.967 --> 35:37.051
Hand it over!

35:37.927 --> 35:39.679
You're being unreasonable!

35:39.762 --> 35:41.055
And you're roadkill.

35:42.598 --> 35:45.226
Wait. Where are you going?

35:45.309 --> 35:48.312
Hey! Fine. I'll just take some change.
I'm only asking for a little, okay?

35:48.396 --> 35:49.480
Huh?

35:52.942 --> 35:54.610
Oh!

35:55.820 --> 36:00.449
You crazy lump of clay!

36:01.033 --> 36:03.828
Why on earth
would your master do this to you?

36:05.913 --> 36:08.291
I asked her for two bucks.

36:08.374 --> 36:10.084
I'd forgive it all if she gave it now.

36:10.168 --> 36:13.087
Oh, what, money? That's what you want?

36:13.171 --> 36:15.798
-It's a thing now.
-Yes, it's become a thing.

36:16.507 --> 36:18.509
-This money really adds up.
-Huh?

36:19.719 --> 36:20.636
You have…

36:21.137 --> 36:23.723
-How do you have all that?
-I work part-time here and there.

36:24.640 --> 36:27.059
Since your master
doesn't give you any money

36:27.143 --> 36:30.646
and ran you over with her car,
then it must be true.

36:30.730 --> 36:32.273
She's nothing but a psychopath.

36:32.356 --> 36:35.651
Oh, interesting. People keep saying
she's on a "path."

36:35.735 --> 36:37.612
What kind of path is it? Do you know?

36:37.695 --> 36:39.197
PSYCHOPATH

36:39.280 --> 36:41.449
"Psychopath" is not a path
you can walk on.

36:42.116 --> 36:44.118
Don't be concerned
with any results that come up.

36:44.785 --> 36:47.330
-Are you prepared for this?
-Not at all.

36:48.706 --> 36:50.958
It feels like they're about
to level up again.

36:53.502 --> 36:55.254
If they knew it was me--

36:56.297 --> 36:59.091
It's just you.

36:59.175 --> 37:02.470
Your jokes are getting better, okay.
But why is the monitor off?

37:02.553 --> 37:03.596
Oh. Look here.

37:07.725 --> 37:08.809
Hmm?

37:10.061 --> 37:11.896
Huh?

37:29.538 --> 37:32.083
Would you like to hear
how disappointed I am

37:32.166 --> 37:34.001
with my good friend Ki Ka-young?

37:35.211 --> 37:37.213
How did I become the last person to know

37:37.296 --> 37:40.007
that you returned from overseas
with a strange guy?

37:40.633 --> 37:41.926
What does this idiot do?

37:42.009 --> 37:44.971
Does he come from money
with a silver spoon in his mouth?

37:46.472 --> 37:48.808
What does he do for a living?
I'm not quite sure yet.

37:51.352 --> 37:53.771
He did tilt the earth to give me a hug.

37:55.064 --> 37:57.525
It's strange he's always asked me
what my wish is.

37:57.608 --> 38:00.403
What kind of wish?
Could he be a cult leader?

38:00.987 --> 38:04.073
Does he mention the rapture often?
Did he ask you for money?

38:04.865 --> 38:07.493
-Yes.
-I knew it. Tell me. How much?

38:08.828 --> 38:10.746
-Just change.
-That's all?

38:11.330 --> 38:14.041
He's that broke? What did you do?

38:14.125 --> 38:17.003
I had to push him off a platform.
Punched him a few times.

38:17.086 --> 38:19.088
I even ran him over with my car.

38:23.384 --> 38:25.011
We're all done for today.

38:26.804 --> 38:29.598
Sounds reasonable. What a broke asshole.

38:30.474 --> 38:32.476
We're all finished. You can go.

38:35.062 --> 38:38.649
I'm just gonna wash my hands
and start with the afternoon appointments.

38:38.733 --> 38:39.817
-Okay.
-All right.

38:41.652 --> 38:45.323
Have you noticed? That person comes here
and lies down to talk.

38:45.406 --> 38:46.949
No work's ever done on her.

38:48.659 --> 38:50.453
I've heard she enjoys
the sound of drilling.

38:50.536 --> 38:52.371
Hmm? So creepy.

38:54.081 --> 38:55.333
I should've guessed.

38:55.416 --> 38:57.960
She had the time of her life
when I took her on a roof

38:58.044 --> 38:59.503
and turned to throw her over.

38:59.587 --> 39:02.048
I didn't stand a chance, did I?

39:02.131 --> 39:05.134
There's nothing to corrupt her with
because she's not like the others.

39:05.217 --> 39:08.596
She was so righteous in her
previous lives. What to do, Master?

39:09.930 --> 39:11.390
I'll just try one more thing.

39:15.061 --> 39:16.937
Let's see if she values
the lives of others.

39:18.939 --> 39:21.067
Next time we drink these aluminum kettles,

39:21.817 --> 39:22.902
we'll be celebrating.

39:52.390 --> 39:54.475
What? That your lighter?

39:55.142 --> 39:57.436
Put that out. We don't want
the whole place to catch fire.

39:58.020 --> 39:59.188
That is your decision.

40:03.067 --> 40:05.486
This fire can't be extinguished
by anyone else.

40:05.569 --> 40:08.072
And I have no interest in putting it out.

40:09.865 --> 40:11.700
Only you can wish for it to stop.

40:52.032 --> 40:54.827
Oh, no! There's a fire!

40:54.910 --> 40:57.663
-A fire!
-Oh! Call 911! Oh, no!

41:01.500 --> 41:03.294
Flames spread quickly.

41:04.295 --> 41:07.590
Are you filming an ad for fire insurance?
Unlock it.

41:07.673 --> 41:11.510
Blaze could engulf the major parts
of the village or much of the city.

41:13.179 --> 41:14.930
Even the entire country, right?

41:21.979 --> 41:23.481
I'm gonna kill you, you idiot.

41:23.981 --> 41:26.942
When I finally come out,
you just blew your only chance.

41:37.161 --> 41:39.955
Wait… What?

41:40.039 --> 41:41.499
What-- Was there another door?

41:41.582 --> 41:44.001
If you had bothered doing your research.

41:44.084 --> 41:45.586
Oh, no, don't. No, no, no.

41:46.170 --> 41:47.004
-No!
-Die!

41:47.087 --> 41:48.881
I kill all jerks who think

41:48.964 --> 41:50.007
they can kill me first!

41:50.090 --> 41:52.051
Why won't you die?

41:52.927 --> 41:54.845
I won't stop until you're dead.

41:57.598 --> 41:59.225
No! Please!

41:59.308 --> 42:02.561
Die!

42:03.395 --> 42:04.480
Ugh! You maniac!

42:04.563 --> 42:06.941
Ow, my butt!

42:08.025 --> 42:10.444
You can wish for the flames to be stopped.
Wish! Wish!

42:10.528 --> 42:12.238
Why would I?

42:12.321 --> 42:14.198
Let it burn to the ground!

42:14.281 --> 42:16.909
I don't care if you want the whole world
to go off in flames.

42:16.992 --> 42:19.787
Ah! Then why do you keep hitting me?

42:19.870 --> 42:21.956
You've ruined my strict nighttime routine.

42:22.456 --> 42:23.541
It's Wednesday today.

42:24.250 --> 42:25.251
Meaning what?

42:25.334 --> 42:29.421
Please stop!

42:37.221 --> 42:38.806
Where are the flames coming from?

42:40.015 --> 42:41.809
I think it started over there.

42:41.892 --> 42:43.227
It couldn't have gone out

42:43.310 --> 42:45.062
-on its own, could it?
-Huh?

42:45.145 --> 42:47.898
-You see the burn marks, don't you?
-I saw the fire too.

42:47.982 --> 42:50.609
Now the flames have all gone out.

42:50.693 --> 42:53.654
While you're here, maybe you could do
something about the assault?

42:53.737 --> 42:55.614
-Right there.
-Whoa! Miss Ki Ka-young!

42:55.698 --> 42:57.741
-Whoa.
-She's not stopping.

43:01.245 --> 43:02.413
Miss Ki Ka-young!

43:02.496 --> 43:04.707
Stop! Police! Drop it!

43:05.207 --> 43:08.168
What's going on? This is so wrong!
You can't beat him like that.

43:08.752 --> 43:11.255
It's no biggie.

43:11.964 --> 43:13.257
I'm not a person at all.

43:13.966 --> 43:16.093
I'm fine, really. I'm fine.

43:16.176 --> 43:18.304
And believe me, I deserve that.

43:18.387 --> 43:20.889
Oh! Your skull! It's been dented.

43:22.391 --> 43:24.977
This is all fine. I feel no pain.

43:25.603 --> 43:27.688
It'll get back once I pull it out.

43:27.771 --> 43:29.315
Your arm is twisted too!

43:30.983 --> 43:32.109
Is it?

43:33.152 --> 43:35.863
Don't worry. It's always like this.

43:35.946 --> 43:38.157
And no need to worry.
Go on your way. I'm fine. Please.

43:38.240 --> 43:40.200
-Thank you.
-With them, you're being polite?

43:41.201 --> 43:43.787
But with me, you're a dick from day one.

43:45.414 --> 43:47.541
Ahhh!

43:48.375 --> 43:51.337
Everyone, leave us. Get out! Let her hit!

43:53.589 --> 43:56.634
It's good for her.
We get along perfectly well.

43:56.717 --> 44:00.429
-We didn't ask anyone to get involved!
-Yup.

44:00.512 --> 44:02.931
This is how it is in today's world.

44:03.015 --> 44:05.768
I'm not going full force
'cause I need to eat gamja-tang now.

44:05.851 --> 44:08.020
If everything
isn't back to normal when I return,

44:08.103 --> 44:09.355
I'll cut you into four pieces

44:09.438 --> 44:11.690
and send them to your maker
at the slowest rate.

44:11.774 --> 44:13.108
Let's start cleaning.

44:13.192 --> 44:15.653
Today, I lost, but I'll do--

44:20.824 --> 44:23.827
As I thought, she doesn't care
about other people's lives.

44:24.912 --> 44:27.039
This was a highly successful effort.

44:27.706 --> 44:31.335
You can't call that a success.
Look at your bruises, Master.

44:31.418 --> 44:33.379
That's fine.

44:33.962 --> 44:35.714
Let's call it "occupational hazard."

44:35.798 --> 44:37.383
I'm warning you.

44:37.466 --> 44:39.176
You lay another hand on me…

44:39.259 --> 44:41.762
-and all people will never--
-All those threats

44:41.845 --> 44:43.597
made no difference to her.

44:44.723 --> 44:47.518
It's not as easy as I thought it would be.
It's been tricky.

44:48.852 --> 44:51.146
I just need to take
a few more punches, that's all.

44:51.230 --> 44:54.525
I think you took a few too many
to the head already.

44:58.028 --> 45:00.197
SA FAMILY GAMJA-TANG

45:01.031 --> 45:05.703
You had a traumatic fire-and-water fight,
yet you can still somehow eat gamja-tang?

45:06.328 --> 45:07.955
-It's Wednesday.
-Yes, it is.

45:08.038 --> 45:10.374
And while we're talking
about the restaurant,

45:10.457 --> 45:12.751
maybe we can eat somewhere else next time.

45:12.835 --> 45:15.295
It's Wednesday night. This is how it is.

45:15.379 --> 45:19.007
-This routine is our friendship.
-Not really. Listen up, all right?

45:19.091 --> 45:21.760
All throughout our years in school,
you took on anyone who hurt me.

45:21.844 --> 45:23.887
-Yes.
-You also cared about my grades

45:23.971 --> 45:25.723
-in literature, languages, and math.
-Yes.

45:25.806 --> 45:27.266
If your grandma passes,

45:27.349 --> 45:29.393
-who's gonna be your first call?
-The village chief.

45:31.437 --> 45:33.480
-That's right. And after him?
-911.

45:34.273 --> 45:35.315
Of course you would.

45:37.025 --> 45:38.235
-And then who?
-You.

45:38.318 --> 45:40.612
That's right. Our friendship works.

45:40.696 --> 45:41.989
Seafood stew next week?

45:44.158 --> 45:47.786
I need gamja-tang every Wednesday!
I follow all of the routines to a tee.

45:47.870 --> 45:50.372
Grandma sets the rules,
this is my routine.

45:50.456 --> 45:52.916
Things go wrong
if one piece falls out of line.

45:53.000 --> 45:56.295
Oh, no. We're not fighting.
Please don't mind us and enjoy.

45:58.547 --> 46:01.884
That's not true, though.
You won't hurt anybody.

46:01.967 --> 46:04.636
You've already proven yourself
in many ways.

46:05.471 --> 46:07.014
That's now, but things change.

46:07.639 --> 46:09.600
And when Grandma does pass on?

46:09.683 --> 46:10.934
Then my rules go away.

46:11.018 --> 46:13.979
And if they go away,
then I could commit murder.

46:14.062 --> 46:15.147
You're not going to.

46:15.230 --> 46:17.483
-You wouldn't do that.
-Do not cut me off!

46:20.110 --> 46:22.863
-I haven't told you the coffin story.
-Okay. Tell me.

46:24.072 --> 46:25.741
How does it start? "A coffin?"

46:25.824 --> 46:27.951
You wanna make a coffin?

46:28.577 --> 46:31.163
Well, I've never made one before, but…

46:31.246 --> 46:34.374
Can we start trying then?
Two coffins with Paulownia wood.

46:34.458 --> 46:36.877
Oh, you wanna build coffins?

46:37.669 --> 46:40.214
For dogs? So how big are they?

46:40.297 --> 46:42.800
Very large, or smaller ones?

46:45.928 --> 46:46.845
How big are you?

46:48.472 --> 46:49.723
She's about your size.

46:49.807 --> 46:51.683
It's not for a dog, for my grandma.

46:51.767 --> 46:54.269
I want a second one for myself.
I'm planning to die

46:54.353 --> 46:56.146
after Grandma passes away.

46:56.230 --> 46:57.648
Mmm.

46:57.731 --> 46:59.817
It'll be as close
to a natural death as possible.

46:59.900 --> 47:01.860
Like some equipment malfunction at sea,

47:01.944 --> 47:04.321
or stumble off
the edge of a trail somewhere.

47:04.404 --> 47:06.865
Those are some options. Do you understand?

47:06.949 --> 47:08.700
I get what you're saying.

47:09.827 --> 47:12.162
But do you have
to tell me about it every time?

47:12.830 --> 47:15.499
-You know I'll be a mess when you die.
-I don't have other friends.

47:15.582 --> 47:18.335
You're the person I tell my secrets to.
You need to keep it together.

47:18.418 --> 47:20.629
Ka-young. Seriously?

47:20.712 --> 47:22.965
Fine.

47:23.048 --> 47:24.758
I'll try to get used to it then.

47:26.051 --> 47:29.012
But you would never, ever murder anyone.

47:31.932 --> 47:33.934
Friends have blind belief in each other.

47:34.017 --> 47:36.603
Is that what you're saying?
I can't do that. Sorry.

47:36.687 --> 47:38.146
I don't care if you can.

47:38.897 --> 47:41.108
Even if you can't do it,
I'll still love you.

47:42.359 --> 47:44.903
So from now on, please, stop it.

47:46.780 --> 47:48.699
-I know.
-What do you know?

47:48.782 --> 47:52.035
I may not know feelings,
but statistics, I do know.

47:52.119 --> 47:54.413
Every Wednesday, I must eat gamja-tang.

47:54.496 --> 47:55.873
Over these last five years,

47:55.956 --> 47:58.208
you've eaten gamja-tang with me
twice a month.

47:58.292 --> 48:01.753
You often don't want to. Yet you always
show up, so I don't eat alone.

48:01.837 --> 48:04.381
You come and sit with me
so others would see that

48:04.464 --> 48:06.884
I'm kind of ordinary,
no different from them.

48:06.967 --> 48:08.135
Mmm.

48:08.844 --> 48:10.345
That's how I know you love me.

48:16.602 --> 48:18.812
I'm gonna get us some water.
Be right back.

48:27.362 --> 48:28.363
Huh?

48:32.242 --> 48:33.869
What the…

48:33.952 --> 48:36.330
What's wrong with this?

48:37.080 --> 48:39.041
-What were you doing in there?
-Huh?

48:39.750 --> 48:42.753
Don't tell me… Were you watching us
from the water filter?

48:42.836 --> 48:46.214
I cleaned the repair store.
I came by to give you the good news.

48:47.007 --> 48:48.091
Oh, you…

48:49.259 --> 48:51.845
Who are you talking to?
Is someone talking to you?

48:52.638 --> 48:54.806
Once again, we're not fighting. We're not.

48:55.807 --> 48:57.225
Keep eating. Keep eating.

48:58.518 --> 48:59.436
Dude!

49:02.356 --> 49:04.858
-Hmm?
-That's three bucks.

49:04.942 --> 49:05.817
You like that thing?

49:07.110 --> 49:08.946
I thought it would look good on you.

49:09.738 --> 49:10.822
Let's go.

49:10.906 --> 49:13.492
-Here's your change.
-Oh, I'll take that. Thank you.

49:20.415 --> 49:21.416
It's yours.

49:23.418 --> 49:26.213
Every time you put this on,
I'll know I'm the only one

49:26.296 --> 49:27.422
who can see you.

49:27.506 --> 49:30.550
Everyone already thinks I'm strange.
I don't need to be even stranger.

49:30.634 --> 49:32.803
It works in my favor if you are.

49:32.886 --> 49:35.597
You have to give me
some incentive to wear this.

49:36.473 --> 49:38.475
The least you could do is make a wish.

49:41.895 --> 49:44.189
Why are you so hung up
on those damn wishes?

49:45.107 --> 49:46.817
Why do you wanna kill me so badly?

49:48.235 --> 49:51.989
What's the point
when you don't remember any of it?

49:52.990 --> 49:55.701
I was stuck in a lamp
for a millennium because of you.

49:56.868 --> 49:58.245
Are you certain it was me?

50:00.747 --> 50:01.665
It was.

50:04.209 --> 50:07.421
Your flesh decayed
and your bones became dust as I watched.

50:07.504 --> 50:09.715
I kept a handful of that dirt, too.

50:11.633 --> 50:13.802
It was difficult to tempt you then,
I'll admit that.

50:13.885 --> 50:15.846
But once you make a wish,
you'll be corrupted,

50:15.929 --> 50:17.889
just like everyone else.

50:18.724 --> 50:20.600
If that's true for all humans,

50:21.184 --> 50:22.310
then people wouldn't call me

50:22.394 --> 50:24.604
a complete psychopath
or anything like that.

50:25.313 --> 50:28.442
I've never even jaywalked
or dumped my trash on the street.

50:29.860 --> 50:32.070
My grandma says folks are generally good,

50:32.154 --> 50:33.864
I've learned I'm what's evil in the world.

50:36.158 --> 50:37.284
You're mistaken.

50:40.454 --> 50:41.663
Not at all.

50:42.330 --> 50:44.916
I've granted wishes
for thousands of years.

50:45.667 --> 50:48.545
They've all ended up corrupted
in one way or another.

50:49.046 --> 50:50.213
Then prove it to me.

50:52.174 --> 50:55.177
How in the world can I prove that
when we're in the middle of a road?

51:00.390 --> 51:01.641
Best three of five.

51:02.309 --> 51:06.063
You'll give the first five people
we meet on this road their wishes.

51:06.146 --> 51:07.981
If three of those individuals

51:08.065 --> 51:09.024
are corrupted,

51:09.816 --> 51:12.903
then I'll make all of my wishes
and die at your hands.

51:14.654 --> 51:16.323
Grandma never lies to me.

51:23.580 --> 51:25.749
Do you know
what you're putting on the line?

51:26.875 --> 51:29.795
-You're not afraid at all?
-Sorry, I don't know how to be afraid.

51:29.878 --> 51:31.755
Take this and hold up
your end of the bargain.

51:32.422 --> 51:34.674
In the meantime,
I intend to be meticulous.

51:34.758 --> 51:37.552
I'll come up with two perfect wishes
that don't have any flaws.

51:37.636 --> 51:38.804
Why would you only make two?

51:40.055 --> 51:42.891
Because I'm making this one.
This is my first wish.

51:44.351 --> 51:45.185
Which is?

51:46.728 --> 51:48.230
I want you to prove it to me.

51:49.064 --> 51:50.941
That all humans are corrupt at heart.

51:52.359 --> 51:53.568
That's my first wish.

52:00.325 --> 52:01.993
You've tempted me, well done.
